-- Chapter 9, Section 9.5.7 — SQL literal-provenance (#309).
-- Features: db_effect, sql_provenance, check_error.
--
-- A DB SQL op whose query string is a runtime value — here the @String
-- parameter — is the SQL injection vector, so Vera rejects it at COMPILE time
-- (E207).  The safe form keeps the SQL literal and passes runtime data through
-- the ? placeholders and the params array.
public fn unsafe(@String -> @Result<Array<Array<Option<String>>>, String>)
  requires(true)
  ensures(true)
  effects(<DB>)
{
  DB.query(@String.0, [])
}
